
---

## 4. Create the GitHub repo

**Two options — pick one.**

### Option A: Create via website (easiest, no tools to install)

1. Open https://github.com/new in your browser
2. **Repository name:** `lumo-ai` (all lowercase, dashes)
3. **Description:** `Every major AI tool — one clean, ad-free app. React Native + Expo.`
4. **Visibility:** Public (recommended — helps with "Hire Me" credibility)
5. ⚠️ **DO NOT** check "Add a README file", "Add .gitignore", or "Choose a license" — you already have those
6. Click **Create repository**
7. GitHub shows you a page with commands — **ignore those**, use the ones below

### Option B: Create via `gh` CLI (needs one-time install)

Skip if you chose Option A.

```bash
# Install once (if you don't have it)
winget install --id GitHub.cli

# Authenticate (opens browser)
gh auth login

# Create the repo and set it as remote
gh repo create lumo-ai --public --source=. --remote=origin --description "Every major AI tool — one clean, ad-free app. React Native + Expo."